//? Title: SHA-256: actual schedules, compression rounds and complete avalanche counts
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Hash complete raw byte messages into a 256-bit digest. Native padded-block and
round histories connect the FIPS construction to its reference vectors before
the original avalanche message experiment.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Append one high bit, zero bits until the byte length is56 modulo64, then the
original64-bit big-endian bit length. Load sixteen big-endian words, expand the
schedule and update the working32-bit state modulo2^32; add the original
chaining words after every block. The report shows actual scheduled words,
working states and feed-forward from this producing execution. Padding can add a
second block when the original length crosses56 modulo64. Avalanche flips each
original input bit independently and counts actual changed digest bits; a mean
near half the digest width is a diagnostic, not evidence of attack resistance.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sha256_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::sha256_trace("abc");
    const auto &b = r.blocks[0];
    std::print("Actual padded bytes {}, incoming chaining words `{}`, outgoing `{}`.\n\n| actual round | " "actual schedule word | actual state after |\n| ---: | ---: | --- |\n",
               r.padded_bytes, b.before, b.after);
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
        const auto &s = b.rounds[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | `{}` |\n", s.index, s.word, s.after);
    }
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Raw bytes abc and FIPS padding");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0}, std::format("Actual rounds {}", r.rounds));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual digest bits 256, blocks {}",
                                     r.compression_blocks));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/sha256_tiny.svg");
}
```
