> API and interpretation

This report verifies a fixed algorithm specification and does not evaluate
current protocol choices or establish attack resistance. Raw bytes include
NUL/high bytes. Complete FIPS length, padded geometry and optional capture
bounds are checked before hashing. The histogram retains every distance from
zero through the full digest width, so tail values are never relabelled into
clipped bins.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [NIST, FIPS180-4 Secure Hash Standard (2015)|https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/180-4/upd1/final]

Verification: 126 scoped native cases;21 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan
cases;124 executable public examples;492/492 full-file definitions and10 exact
Sfc64 members;10 hovers;1588 independent records/14377 checks;frozen comparisons
across all ten families with endpoint/full-width field corrections recorded;17
checkout/installed standalone headers and linked/umbrella consumers;40 executed
programs and40 inspected figures with both exports. The complete
original4000-step native tensor SOM trajectory agrees with an independent NumPy
replay, including every winner and final assignment. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-344-353/`.
